{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>If Cain shall be avenged sevenfold.</b> Cain, who killed intentionally — it was suspended for him until seven generations. I, who killed unintentionally — all the more so that it should be suspended for me many times seven!" "<b>Seventy-sevenfold.</b> A term of multiplying sevens — thus did Rabbi Tanchuma expound. And the midrash of Bereshit Rabbah: Lemech killed no one at all. His wives separated from him and refrained from fulfilling פְּרִיָּה וּרְבִיָּה, because a decree had been issued to wipe out the seed of Cain after seven generations. They said: What are we bearing children for in vain? Tomorrow the Flood comes and washes away everything! And he said to them: Did I kill a man for my wound? Did I kill Abel — who was a fully grown man and a youth in years — so that my seed should perish on account of that? And what Cain, who killed, was suspended seven generations — I, who did not kill, all the more so that they should suspend for me many times seven! And this is an a fortiori argument of folly. If so, the Holy One, blessed be He, does not exact His debt and fulfill His word."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:35.376689720Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}